{#
_pane_window_controls.html.twig — the end of a docked pane's header: full
width or back beside the mail, and close (#678).

The calendar pane and the address book are the same kind of thing, a pane
docked beside the mail with three positions, and they had two different ends:
the address book an ↗ and an ×, the calendar nothing at all, so the only way
to close it or give it the row was the topbar switch. And at full width
neither had a way back, because the address book's pair was hidden there.
One partial for both, so the next pane gets the same pair without anybody
having to remember it.

    {% include '_partials/_pane_window_controls.html.twig' with {
        controller:   'ui--split',          the controller with expand, restore
                                            and close (ui--split for the
                                            calendar, contacts--pane for the
                                            address book)
        expandUrl:    path(…),              the full-size page, for a middle or
                                            modified click, which is a new tab
        expandLabel:  '…'|trans,
        restoreLabel: '…'|trans,
        closeLabel:   '…'|trans,
    } only %}

Expand and restore are both rendered and app.css shows one of them, keyed on
the position the shell is in (`data-calendar-mode`, `data-contacts-full`), so
the right one is there on the first paint without a controller having to swap
icons. Below lg neither is: the pane already has the row there, and there is
no "beside" to go back to. Close is there at every width.

After a thin rule, so the pair reads as the window's and not as two more of the
page's actions.
#}

<span data-pane-window-controls class="flex items-center gap-0.5 shrink-0 pl-1 ml-0.5 border-l border-line">
    <a href="{{ expandUrl }}"
       data-pane-expand
       data-turbo-frame="_top"
       data-action="{{ controller }}#expand"
       class="icon-btn"
       aria-label="{{ expandLabel }}"
       title="{{ expandLabel }}">
        <i class="fa-solid fa-up-right-and-down-left-from-center text-xs" aria-hidden="true"></i>
    </a>
    <button type="button"
            data-pane-restore
            data-action="{{ controller }}#restore"
            class="icon-btn"
            aria-label="{{ restoreLabel }}"
            title="{{ restoreLabel }}">
        <i class="fa-solid fa-down-left-and-up-right-to-center text-xs" aria-hidden="true"></i>
    </button>
    <button type="button"
            data-pane-close
            data-action="{{ controller }}#close"
            class="icon-btn"
            aria-label="{{ closeLabel }}"
            title="{{ closeLabel }}">
        <i class="fa-solid fa-xmark text-sm" aria-hidden="true"></i>
    </button>
</span>
